    "required": false,
    "value": "No — Pennsylvania's constitution bars anyone convicted of embezzlement of public moneys, bribery, perjury, or other infamous crime from the General Assembly or from holding any office of trust or profit in the Commonwealth, but the U.S. Constitution's own qualifications for Congress (age, citizenship, residency) can't be added to by any state, so this doesn't reach U.S. House or Senate candidates",
